{
  "version": 1,

  "_comment": "Starter pack manifest for the cross-stream editing library. This file is METADATA ONLY - no audio or images are committed to this repository. `python -m clipbot library fetch` reads it and downloads into work/_library/, which is gitignored.",

  "_comment_empty": "The assets list ships empty on purpose. Every entry must carry a REAL sha256, and a wrong one is worse than a missing entry: fetch would reject the file and you would be debugging a hash instead of editing a clip. Pixabay and Freesound both hand out their download URLs from client-side API calls rather than the page HTML, so the URLs cannot be harvested reliably or durably - and a manifest full of guessed hashes would fail on every single entry. Add entries yourself with the recipe below; it takes about fifteen seconds each.",

  "_comment_howto": [
    "1. Find a CC0 / public-domain sound. Good sources, all free for monetised streams:",
    "     https://pixabay.com/sound-effects/   (Pixabay Content Licence - no attribution, commercial OK)",
    "     https://freesound.org/  (filter the search by Creative Commons 0)",
    "   Search terms that cover most stream-reel edits: vine boom, airhorn, bruh, bonk,",
    "   record scratch, whoosh, riser, impact, sub drop, error, crowd cheer, sad trombone.",
    "2. Download it and drop it straight into work/_library/sfx/ - that alone is enough to",
    "   start using it. This manifest only exists so a library can be rebuilt from scratch",
    "   on another machine.",
    "3. To record it here, get the hash and size with:",
    "     python -m clipbot library hash <path-to-file>",
    "   then paste the printed block into the assets array below and fill in url + license.",
    "4. `python -m clipbot library fetch` will then reproduce it anywhere, verifying the",
    "   hash as it downloads. `python -m clipbot library licenses` prints provenance for",
    "   everything in the library."
  ],

  "_comment_hosts": "url must be https and its host must appear in library.fetch.allow_hosts in config/settings.json. That allowlist exists because this file is data: without it, editing a manifest would be enough to make ClipBot fetch from anywhere.",

  "_schema": {
    "slug": "short unique id used by --only, e.g. \"airhorn\"",
    "kind": "sfx | music | sticker | font",
    "url": "https URL on an allowlisted host",
    "filename": "name it lands under, e.g. \"airhorn.mp3\" - no path separators",
    "bytes": "expected size; the download aborts past 2x this",
    "sha256": "REQUIRED and must be real - a mismatch fails this asset cleanly",
    "name": "display name in the effects drawer",
    "tags": ["searchable", "labels"],
    "license": {
      "name": "CC0-1.0",
      "author": "who made it",
      "source": "page you got it from",
      "url": "licence text"
    }
  },

  "_example": {
    "slug": "airhorn",
    "kind": "sfx",
    "url": "https://cdn.pixabay.com/download/audio/2022/03/15/audio_0000000000.mp3",
    "filename": "airhorn.mp3",
    "bytes": 41234,
    "sha256": "replace-with-the-real-hash-from-library-hash",
    "name": "Airhorn",
    "tags": ["hype", "horn"],
    "license": {
      "name": "CC0-1.0",
      "author": "",
      "source": "https://pixabay.com/sound-effects/airhorn-0000/",
      "url": "https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/"
    }
  },

